# B4 fixtures are CONTENT-ADDRESSED: the file name IS the sha256 of the
# file's own bytes. Any end-of-line conversion (core.autocrlf normalises
# LF→CRLF on checkout for text files) would change those bytes and break
# the name ⇔ digest binding, silently invalidating every fixture on a
# fresh clone. These files are therefore explicitly NON-TEXT: git stores
# and checks them out byte-for-byte, on every platform.
*.json -text
